LocalStack — AWS Local Development

LocalStack allows me to run and test AWS services locally using Docker instead of deploying everything directly into a live AWS environment.

Current Tool Stack

* LocalStack
* Docker Desktop
* AWS CLI
* PowerShell
* Git / GitHub

What I’m Using It For

* Practicing AWS CLI commands
* Creating and managing AWS resources locally
* Testing cloud configurations
* Troubleshooting AWS environments
* Learning infrastructure and security concepts
* Building repeatable cloud labs
* Documenting my progress and solutions

Current Focus

Moving beyond the AWS console and getting more hands-on experience with the CLI, infrastructure configuration, troubleshooting, and automation.

Goal: Build → Break → Troubleshoot → Fix → Document → Repeat.